# Registry of every patch this repo carries against upstream.
#
# ONE source of truth, read by two consumers:
#   - ci/check-patch-registry.sh          per-PR: every carried patch has a row,
#                                         and every row still describes something
#                                         carried
#   - .github/workflows/tailscale-upstream-watch.yml
#                                         weekly: has each row's upstream fix
#                                         merged AND shipped yet
#
# fields: file|kind|repo|number
#
#   file    a filename in tailscale/patches/, or an `@id` for a patch applied
#           inline by tailscale/build-tailscalekit.sh (no .patch file exists).
#           An `@id` must match a `# PATCH-REGISTRY: @id` marker in that script.
#   kind    manual   retirement is a human decision; nothing upstream gates it
#           merge    retires when the upstream PR MERGES
#           release  retires when a RELEASE carries the fix. Not the same as
#                    merge: #20985 merged 2026-08-26 and is still absent from
#                    v1.102.3 and v1.103.0-pre. Confusing the two is a bug in
#                    both directions — one carries a patch for months, the other
#                    deletes a patch whose fix is not in the pinned version.
#   repo    upstream repo under github.com/tailscale/ (blank for kind=manual)
#   number  upstream PR number (blank for kind=manual)
#
# This registry describes what is carried NOW, not what was ever carried. 0002
# (libtailscale#58, merged 61e8513) and 0003 (libtailscale#60, merged 8564835)
# were retired on 2026-08-31 by bumping the submodule past both and DELETING the
# patch files, so their rows are gone too. ci/check-patch-registry.sh is what
# keeps the file list and this list in step, in both directions.

0001-tailscalekit-nslog-tracing.patch|manual||
@module-cache-bus-guard|release|tailscale|20985
